# Keep the Docker build context (and image) slim: ship ONLY the ~5.6 GB of model
# artifacts + 2 serving CSVs that are loaded at runtime. Everything below is training
# data, intermediate files, or model families that were replaced (Model A/B) and are
# NOT loaded by the live server.

# ── version control / caches / editor ──
.git/
.gitignore
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log

# ── notebooks (training/conversion only) ──
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── training datasets & intermediate CSVs (not used at runtime) ──
data/merged_sentiment.csv
data/tweets.csv
data/IMDB Dataset.csv
data/fake reviews dataset.csv
data/yelp_split.csv
data/yelp_split_imbalanced.csv
data/yelp_multimodal_features.csv
data/yelp_multimodal_augmented.csv
data/review_detection.csv
data/non_reviews.csv
data/yelp_frontend_reviews.csv
data/amazon_top100_results.csv
data/ai_*.csv
data/fake_reviews_broadened.csv
data/*_results.csv

# ── raw Yelp dumps (used only to build the frontend CSV) ──
data/YelpZip*/
data/YelpNYC*/
data/YelpChi*/

# ── model families replaced by Model A / Model B (kept on disk locally for eval) ──
# Amazon-only fake detector -> replaced by Model A (broadened)
data/fake_*.joblib
data/fake_lstm.onnx
data/fake_lstm_tokenizer.json
data/fake_distilbert_onnx/
# Yelp text-only baseline + focal/contrastive ablations -> replaced by Model B
data/yelp_fake_sklearn_models/
data/yelp_fake_lstm_onnx/
data/yelp_fake_distilbert_onnx/
data/yelp_fake_lstm_focal_onnx/
data/yelp_fake_distilbert_focal_onnx/
data/yelp_fake_lstm_contrastive_onnx/
data/yelp_fake_distilbert_contrastive_onnx/
# Model B Model-#1 fusion variants (local-only, not served)
data/yelp_multimodal_fusion_models/
data/yelp_multimodal_generalized_models/

# ── runtime-created / local-only ──
data/users.db

# model backups (e.g. the depth-bounded-RF .bak files) — keep them locally if you like,
# but never ship them: they're never loaded and would just bloat the image/transfer.
*.bak
**/*.bak
